{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Speak to Aaron.</b> The portion of the priests, who are holy, is juxtaposed to the portion of the nazirite, who is holy when he completes the law of his naziriteship." "<b>And to his sons.</b> This teaches that the lifting of the hands is performed even by an ordinary priest." "<b>Thus you shall bless.</b> In the first year, when they were encamped in one place, the Canaanites did not notice them. But in the second year, when they set up standards and trumpets for the needs of the journeys, the Canaanites said: now they are coming to fight us. Then they needed the priestly blessing, lest the enemies come upon them because of sin and do battle with Israel and take captives from them. Thus you shall bless — standing, as it is said, אלה יעמדו לברך." "<b>Say to them.</b> This teaches that the cantor must say to them: 'Recite!' And so it is translated: כד תימרון להון. From here that a priest does not transgress a positive commandment if he does not ascend to the platform until they command him."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:49.266189261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}